---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { directoryStats, href, partnerUrl } from '../lib/data';
import { breadcrumbNode, pageGraph, webPageNode } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'Affiliate disclosure and privacy';
const description =
  'How commercial links to Neighbor and SpareFoot work, and what this static directory stores about visitors.';
const path = '/disclosure/';
const crumbs = [
  { label: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { label: 'Disclosure', path },
];
const schema = pageGraph([
  webPageNode({ title, description, path, dateModified: directoryStats().latest }),
  breadcrumbNode(crumbs),
]);
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path={path} schema={schema}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure and privacy</h1>
    <h2>Commercial links</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages link to
      <a href={partnerUrl('neighbor')} rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">Neighbor</a>
      and
      <a href={partnerUrl('sparefoot')} rel="sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer">SpareFoot</a>.
      Those links are commercial. They are marked with <code>rel="sponsored nofollow"</code>. Affiliate
      accounts are not approved yet, so the links open the companies’ public pages and do not add a
      tracking id. If an id is added later, a visit or a booking through that link may earn this site a
      commission. That commission would not change the facility price you are quoted.
    </p>
    <p>
      The configuration for those URLs and the empty affiliate ids lives in
      <code>src/data/site.yaml</code>. Facility names, phones, and websites are not paid placements.
      A business cannot buy a higher spot on a city page.
    </p>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={href('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> is the full note. In short, this directory is a
      static site. It has no accounts and does not collect visitor data itself. GitHub Pages may log
      requests in order to deliver the files. An affiliate site you open may set its own cookies.
    </p>
    <p>
      A link to a facility, to Google Maps, or to a marketplace leaves this site. The next site has its
      own policy. Phone links open your own dialer and do not pass through us.
    </p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Storage prices and amenities change. The date on each card is the day the source was opened. If a
      fact is wrong, the correction belongs in that city’s YAML file with a new source check, using the
      steps in PUBLISHING.md. Opening a GitHub issue on the repository is a fine way to flag one.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
